/* SPDX-License-Identifier: 0BSD
 * Provenance: original pcrec-memory-functions text; no third-party source
 *   (memfn/PROVENANCE.md).
 *
 * memfn/src/options.def — THE KIT'S OPTION REGISTRY (D147 addendum 9;
 * integration.md §R4.4.1). An X-macro in axes.def's and limits.def's idiom,
 * but the kit's own: pcrec's build never reads it and pcrec's sources never
 * include it. options.c includes it for the table behind mf_options() and
 * for the parser behind mf_opts_check(), so what `--list-axes`' `memfn`
 * section prints and what `--memfn=` accepts are one table.
 *
 * MF_OPT(name, kind, budget, layer, doc)
 *   name    kit-owned id, [a-z0-9-], arch-blind (C4)
 *   kind    MF_OPT_DENY | MF_OPT_PAIR    which --memfn= spellings it takes:
 *           `no-NAME` always; a bare `NAME` (force) only for MF_OPT_PAIR
 *   budget  MF_B_SCAN | MF_B_LOOP | MF_B_ANY       D91, as §8.5's INLOOP
 *   layer   MF_L_SCALAR | MF_L_SIMD      which acceptance reading owns it
 *           (§L.4); an MF_L_SIMD row is inert at -fno-memfn-simd
 *   doc     one line
 *
 * A kit change that moves an emitted byte adds its row HERE in the same
 * commit (D144 item 4): the row is that change's OFF arm, `--memfn=no-NAME`,
 * and the change raises the `memfn` section's floor in docs/spec/registry.md
 * §6. BORN EMPTY at R4a: no kit form moves a byte yet, so there is no row,
 * and the floor check is UNREACHED until the first row (R4d).
 */
